    {
      "_id": "9aa8d9361a1b44af",
      "name": "GM Reference: Nan Gristle, Voice and Signal Loft",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>Nan Gristle, Trolley Signalwoman</h2><p><em>\"Four slow means stop and wait. Everybody knows that. Well. Everybody up here.\"</em></p><p><strong>Body:</strong> a broad old half-orc woman with a brass speaking-trumpet on a strap, signal flags in her apron, and a bell on a post beside her chair. Fully her own body, and proud of it.</p><p><strong>Job:</strong> signals the overhead bone trolleys through the Lower market interchange from a loft above the rails (the Ropewalk and Signal Loft, above Haddo's workshop).</p><p><strong>Not in the Thaw.</strong> She helps because she likes the party, enjoys Lil (the ducks rode her trolleys for an afternoon), and dislikes Tallis riding her tenth-hour trolley and timing it. She barely knows Quill (\"the skinny one with the chalk\") and thinks the dusty terminal is \"Pell's hobby\".</p><p><strong>Voice:</strong> loud, cheerful, nosy; talks through the trumpet even when you're next to her. Taps the bell rope when nervous.</p><h3>Sample dialogue</h3><ul><li>[COMMON] <em>(through the trumpet)</em> \"MIND THE BASKETS. Oh, you're right there. Mind the baskets.\"</li><li>[COMMON] \"Four slow on my bell means stop and wait. Two fast means go. Easy.\"</li><li>[ASK] \"Inspector Tallis rides the tenth-hour trolley every night now. Times it with his watch. Rude.\"</li><li>[ASK] \"Want to borrow the bell? Bring it back with its tongue in. People keep stealing tongues lately.\"</li><li>[ASK] \"I can hold the tenth-hour a few minutes. Signal fault. Happens all the time. Happens when I say it happens.\"</li><li>[EARN] \"I don't want to know what you're doing. I want to know if it's going to be funny.\"</li></ul><p><strong>Quest hooks:</strong> lends the signal bell for the test pull (T6); can delay Tallis (Scene 5).</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide, Part 7 (Session 14)",
          "book": "",
          "page": "",
          "license": "",
          "rules": "2014",
          "revision": 1
        },
